WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.425
How does BIND forward?

2
00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:05.513
The native resolver stays the only
path to the cloud's own names.

3
00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:08.063
BIND's forward setting defaults to first,

4
00:00:08.063 --> 00:00:11.738
which falls back to its own
recursion when forwarders fail.

5
00:00:11.738 --> 00:00:16.493
For private names, that fallback can
return the public answer or NXDOMAIN,

6
00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:20.625
so the AWS whitepaper says it's
critical to specify forward only.

7
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:23.002
Per-instance limits: on AWS,

8
00:00:23.002 --> 00:00:29.919
the 1,024-packet-per-second quota covers
everything BIND sends to VPC plus two;

9
00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:33.917
on Azure, a VM may send
1,000 queries per second,

10
00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:37.375
and queries over the limit are dropped.

11
00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:40.737
Size the fleet so no server
forwards near the limit.

12
00:00:40.737 --> 00:00:44.587
Visibility: the VPC Resolver
sees BIND as the source,

13
00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:47.899
never the client, so BIND's
logs are the record.

14
00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:50.754
And loops: don't forward
a domain to an inbound

15
00:00:50.754 --> 00:00:53.830
endpoint from inside the
network that holds it.
